    <td align=right bgcolor="#6E94B7"><nobr>&nbsp;<font class="text1" color="#FFFFFF" size=2>on: Jan 22<sup>nd</sup>, 2003, 9:34am&nbsp;</font></nobr></td>
  </tr><tr>
    <td colspan=3 bgcolor="#DEE7EF" class="catbg"><font class="catbg" size=2>Started by <a href="http://www.eq-eod.com/cgi-bin/yabb/YaBB.pl?action=viewprofile;username=Tomah" alt="View Profile: Tomah">Tomah</a> | Last post by <a href="http://www.eq-eod.com/cgi-bin/yabb/YaBB.pl?action=viewprofile;username=Tomah" alt="View Profile: Tomah">Tomah</a></font></td>
  </tr><tr height=80>
    <td colspan=3 bgcolor="#D8F8F8" valign=top><font size=2>I just wanted to remind everyone that we're still part of GCP and that they have raids and groups doing something almost every single night as well. <br> &nbsp;<br> Also, if you look on the EverquestRaids board, follow the link at the top, our guild is &quot;invited&quot; to a raid about twice a week by other GCP guilds, for GCP only type events. &nbsp; <br> &nbsp;<br> Many times, it's the same group of people we have played with in the past and continue to, although seems like not as much. <br> &nbsp;<br> Please, take the time to register your char on the board, and join these raids if interested and time permits. <br> &nbsp;<br> This doesn't even include all the open to everyone raids that still seem to be hosted in part by the same people. <br> &nbsp;<br> So, between what we do as a guild and our participation in GCP, there should be something interesting to do every single day. <br> &nbsp;<br> Tomah </font></td>
  </tr><tr>
    <td colspan=3 bgcolor="#DEE7EF"><font size=2>&nbsp;
